\ The first structural choices after selecting the requested year.
\ All structure questions use one sauce pair:
\   (calculation day, first day of the selected year).
\ The year's first day is opening gate plus one calendar day.
\ Bowl 2, seal 20 selects how many cutlets (6..min(17,G)),
\ where G is the number of gate intervals in the year.
\ Bowl 3, seal 30 selects how many months, 3..47, subject to
\ 4..123 calendar days for each month and the exact year length.
\ Both choices are uniformly mapped with the canonical equal-choice
\ mechanism, not ordinary modulo without rejection.
\ This file does not assign cutlet lengths, names or month weaving.
\ CAL compilation has not yet been verified.

A structural count range has
  a number called first option,
  a number called last option,
  a number called option count.

The cutlet count range is a structural count range.
The month count range is a structural count range.
The selected cutlet count is a number.
The selected month count is a number.

\ G is the year candidate's span count, never its length in days.
To prepare the cutlet count range:
  Put 6 into the cutlet count range's first option.
  Put the chosen year's span count into the cutlet count range's last option.
  If the cutlet count range's last option is greater than 17,
    put 17 into the cutlet count range's last option.
  Put the cutlet count range's last option into the cutlet count range's option count.
  Subtract 5 from the cutlet count range's option count.

\ For positive year length L, floor((L+122)/123) is ceil(L/123).
\ The largest permitted month count is min(47,floor(L/4)).
To prepare the month count range:
  Put the chosen year's year length into the month count range's first option.
  Add 122 to the month count range's first option.
  Divide the month count range's first option by 123.
  Put the chosen year's year length into the month count range's last option.
  Divide the month count range's last option by 4.
  If the month count range's last option is greater than 47,
    put 47 into the month count range's last option.
  Put the month count range's last option into the month count range's option count.
  Subtract the month count range's first option from the month count range's option count.
  Add 1 to the month count range's option count.

\ Keep the chosen structural sauce in the current bowls until all
\ choices for the same year have finished. No gate query may overwrite it.
To prepare the year structure sauce:
  Put the year selection day into the example's calculation day.
  Put the chosen year's opening day into the example's requested day.
  Add 1 to the example's requested day.
  Answer the example.
  Copy the example into the sauce input.
  Make the complete sauce.

\ For a range [a,b], the accepted option is a-1+choice in 1..b-a+1.
To choose the cutlet count:
  Prepare the cutlet count range.
  Put 2 into the seal inquiry's bowl identity.
  Put 20 into the seal inquiry's seal number.
  Begin a seal inquiry.
  Convert the cutlet count range's option count to a string.
  Put the string into a structural options wide quantity.
  Choose an equal option given the structural options wide quantity.
  Convert the seal inquiry's selected quantity to the selected cutlet count.
  Add the cutlet count range's first option to the selected cutlet count.
  Subtract 1 from the selected cutlet count.

\ The month count uses the SAME bowls but its own seal and identity.
To choose the month count:
  Prepare the month count range.
  Put 3 into the seal inquiry's bowl identity.
  Put 30 into the seal inquiry's seal number.
  Begin a seal inquiry.
  Convert the month count range's option count to a string.
  Put the string into a structural options wide quantity.
  Choose an equal option given the structural options wide quantity.
  Convert the seal inquiry's selected quantity to the selected month count.
  Add the month count range's first option to the selected month count.
  Subtract 1 from the selected month count.

\ A caller first locates the requested year, then makes one sauce.
To choose the structural counts:
  Prepare the year structure sauce.
  Choose the cutlet count.
  Choose the month count.
